Mini Vector AML

This compact implementation follows the non-graph open-source memory workflow
of mem0 (https://github.com/mem0ai/mem0), described in: Prateek Chhikara, Dev
Khant, Saket Aryan, Taranjeet Singh, Deshraj Yadav, "Mem0: Building
Production-Ready AI Agents with Scalable Long-Term Memory", arXiv:2504.19413,
2025. The upstream project is licensed under Apache License 2.0. Its license is
preserved in third_party/mem0/LICENSE and includes the original notice:
Copyright [2023] [Taranjeet Singh].

Attribution reference: mem0 commit 47a69e1e72dc562b6fdd49a9ef892229afc7508a.
That reference identifies the locally inspected upstream snapshot; it does not
claim that this repository is an unmodified checkout of that commit.

Changes from the upstream workflow (baseline-v1):
- compact synchronous Python API with SQLite persistence and exact vector scans;
- FTS5 BM25 retrieval; ADD-only fact extraction (no UPDATE/DELETE decisions);
- AML-specific authenticated Add/Search adapter with atomic batch ingestion,
  durable idempotency, exact user isolation and Qwen text-embedding-v4.

Additional changes in enhanced-v2 (own work unless noted):
- memory-side retrieval questions generated per fact and indexed as vectors;
- query decomposition into up to three subqueries, each searched separately;
- equal-weight reciprocal rank fusion (k=60) over all retrieval routes;
- qwen3-rerank (Alibaba Cloud DashScope text rerank API) over the fused head,
  with a fixed instruction, falling back to the fused order on failure;
- concurrency: per-user serialization instead of a global lock, provider calls
  outside the storage transaction, incrementally maintained per-user vector
  pools, parallel question-generation groups and embedding batches, and bounded
  provider retries. Thread-pool fan-out of independent calls follows the pattern
  used in mem0's search path.

Additional changes in the final submitted configuration (own work), enabled by
command-line switches on the enhanced-v2 code (see README):
- time_v2 extraction prompt: only the time-related text of the mem0-derived
  extraction prompt is revised (precision-preserving resolution of relative
  times against the observation date, observation anchors for unresolved
  wording, observation date not used as event date; three examples corrected);
- `list` qwen3-rerank instruction, favoring every memory that contributes a
  distinct item or necessary link for list, count, comparison and multi-part
  questions; selected among six frozen candidate instructions;
- observation-date prefix on Search content, derived from Add message timestamps.
These choices were compared offline on one public LoCoMo conversation (conv-26);
no benchmark data, questions, answers or names are included in the repository.

The ordered-query validation pattern comes from the author's own query-rewrite
research. The short-ID listwise contract in retrieval.py (used only by the
optional LLM rerank modes, not by the default qwen mode) is adapted from the
author's mini-hindsight, a compact reimplementation of Hindsight by Vectorize AI
(https://github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight, MIT License); no Hindsight source is
included. This repository does not distribute mem0's full source tree,
benchmark data, experiment outputs or credentials.
